# Security overrides for the Hermes gateway venv (/opt/hermes/.venv).
#
# Each line moves ONE package that Hermes' own uv.lock (at the Dockerfile's
# HERMES_UPSTREAM_SHA) installs, to the release that fixes a named advisory.
# Everything else in that venv stays exactly at the version Hermes locked.
# compile.sh resolves this file together with the rest of Hermes' locked set,
# so a line here cannot pick a version some other Hermes package refuses;
# the image installs the result (hermes-security.txt) with --require-hashes
# right after `uv sync`, and hermes_pip_check.py then proves the venv is
# consistent.
#
# Admission rule: an override is near zero-risk to Hermes or it does not go
# here. A fix that changes an API Hermes calls, or that Hermes exact-pins on
# purpose (PyJWT), is a Hermes promotion (move HERMES_UPSTREAM_SHA through its
# own rehearsal), and its advisories sit in .github/pip-audit-allowlist.json
# until that promotion lands. pip_audit_gate.py audits the venv's effective
# set (Hermes' lock with these overrides applied), so nothing in it is unseen.
#
# Remove a line once Hermes' lock at HERMES_UPSTREAM_SHA carries the fix.

# brotlicffi 1.2.0.2 -> fix: PYSEC-2026-4323 / GHSA-9v8h-qqgm-4m35 (out-of-bounds
# write in the Brotli decoder). Reachable: aiohttp decodes a `br` response body
# with it. A patch release of a binding with no API change Hermes calls.
# hermes-agent exact-pins brotlicffi==1.2.0.2 in its `messaging` extra
# (pyproject.toml, v0.22.5), so hermes_pip_check.py tolerates that one
# requirement, and only while the installed version is the pin below.
brotlicffi>=1.2.1.0
